# FigureForge is built and run entirely inside Linux containers — the shell
# scripts, Dockerfiles and Makefile are read by the container, never by native
# Windows tooling. Git for Windows converts text files to CRLF on checkout by
# default, which turns a script's `#!/usr/bin/env bash` shebang into `bash\r`
# and stops the web container from starting. Force LF on every platform.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# Guard rails for asset types that could be added later — keep git from ever
# treating one as text and rewriting its bytes.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.eps           binary
*.tif           binary
*.tiff          binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.ffg           binary
*.figureforge   binary
*.xlsx          binary
*.prism         binary
